This behavior is not a bug; it is expected when Strict Mode is enabled. In development, React runs an extra setup and cleanup cycle for every Effect to help identify issues. This means your Effect will connect, disconnect, and then connect again, which is a stress-test to verify the Effect's logic [3].

To ensure this behavior is harmless, you should include a cleanup function in your Effect that properly disconnects the connection when the Effect is re-run. This way, the cleanup function will stop or undo whatever the setup function was doing, preventing any unintended side effects [3]. 

Here’s an example of how to structure your Effect:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const connection = createConnection(serverUrl, roomId);
  connection.connect();
  return () => connection.disconnect(); // Cleanup function
}, [roomId]);
```

By adding the cleanup function, you ensure that the previous connection is properly closed before a new one is established, thus avoiding any potential issues with multiple active connections [1][2].

